<%# Generic starting-point Privacy Policy, written to match what this app actually
    stores (see db/schema.rb). Reviewed by no lawyer — have counsel read it, and
    update it whenever the data model changes. Bump PagesController::LAST_UPDATED. %>
<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy — #{@service_name}" %>

<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 sm:py-14">
  <header class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">
      Last updated <%= @last_updated.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        <%= @service_name %> (the "Service") is operated by <%= @operator %> ("we", "us"). This policy
        explains what information the Service collects, why, and what we do with it. The Service is a
        private, invitation-only tool used to plan and publish our own social media content; it is not
        a consumer product open to public sign-up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">2. Information we collect</h2>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Account information</h3>
      <p>Your name, email address, and a hashed (never plaintext) password.</p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Session information</h3>
      <p>
        When you sign in we record the session, including the IP address and browser user agent, so
        you can stay signed in and so we can detect unauthorized access.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Connected platform credentials</h3>
      <p>
        When you connect Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, or TikTok, we store the access and refresh
        tokens those platforms issue, their expiry times, and the account identifiers and usernames
        they return. These tokens let the Service publish on your behalf. We do not receive or store
        your password for any connected platform.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Media and content</h3>
      <p>
        Images and video you add to the Service, along with captions, hashtags, scheduling
        information, and technical metadata such as file size, dimensions, duration, and format.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Location data in media</h3>
      <p>
        Photos often carry GPS coordinates in their EXIF metadata. Where present, the Service reads
        those coordinates and converts them into a human-readable place name (address, city, state,
        country) to help organize your library. You can remove this data by editing or deleting the
        media asset.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">People recognition</h3>
      <p>
        The Service can analyze images to identify which people from your own saved list of known
        people appear in them, so posts can be organized and captioned. This analysis produces labels
        stored alongside the media asset. It is used only within your account and is never used to
        identify strangers or shared for advertising.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-medium text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-1">Assistant conversations</h3>
      <p>
        If you use the built-in assistant, we store your messages, its responses, and records of the
        actions it took, so conversations persist between visits.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">3. How we use information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>to operate the Service and publish content you schedule;</li>
        <li>to authenticate you and keep your account secure;</li>
        <li>to retrieve engagement metrics for posts you have published;</li>
        <li>to organize and search your media library;</li>
        <li>to diagnose failures and improve reliability.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We do not sell your information, use it for advertising, or use it to build profiles of
        anyone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">4. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We share information only with service providers that make the Service work:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1">
        <li>
          <strong>Meta, Google, and TikTok</strong> — content, captions, and metadata you choose to
          publish are sent to whichever platform you are publishing to, under the permissions you
          granted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>DigitalOcean</strong> — hosting and media file storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI model providers</strong> — when you use the assistant or automated media
          analysis, the relevant text or images are sent to the model provider to generate a response.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Geocoding providers</strong> — coordinates from media metadata are sent to a
          geocoding service to resolve a place name.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect our rights or the safety of
        others.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">5. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep information for as long as your account is active. Media assets, planned posts, and
        conversations remain until you delete them. Disconnecting a platform deletes the stored tokens
        for that platform. Deleting your account removes your account record and the content
        associated with it. Content already published to a third-party platform is governed by that
        platform and must be removed there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Traffic is encrypted in transit over HTTPS. Passwords are stored using a one-way hash.
        Platform tokens are stored in our database and filtered out of application logs, and access to
        the Service is limited to invited accounts. No system is perfectly secure, and we cannot
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">7. Your choices</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Disconnect any social media platform at any time from the admin area.</li>
        <li>Revoke our access directly in your Instagram, Facebook, Google, or TikTok account settings.</li>
        <li>Edit or delete individual media assets, planned posts, and conversations.</li>
        <li>
          Request a copy of your information or deletion of your account by emailing
          <%= mail_to @contact_email, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" %>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">8. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information
        from them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected in the "Last
        updated" date above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about this policy can be sent to
        <%= mail_to @contact_email, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-500">
    See also our <%= link_to "Terms of Service", tos_path, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 hover:underline" %>.
  </footer>
</article>
